  "description": {
    "text": "Basic Energy cards with a ©2005 line and no set symbol or collection number, in six types. They keep the Energy painting of EX Ruby & Sapphire but drop the e-Reader mark from the bottom left corner, as the EX Trainer Kit's Energy had first done.\n\nEnglish theme decks of the EX years carried them in place of numbered Energy. Collectors comparing deck openings found ©2005 Energy in the theme decks of EX Deoxys, EX Emerald, EX Unseen Forces, EX Crystal Guardians, EX Dragon Frontiers and EX Power Keepers.",
    "sources": [
      {
        "title": "Elite Fourum: Where do setless (c) 2006 EX-era Basic Energy come from?",
        "url": "https://www.elitefourum.com/t/where-do-setless-c-2006-ex-era-basic-energy-come-from/31244"
      },
      {
        "title": "Bulbapedia: Basic Fire Energy (TCG) (Wayback Machine copy, 1 September 2026)",
        "url": "https://web.archive.org/web/20260901020457/https://bulbapedia.bulbagarden.net/wiki/Fire_Energy_(TCG)"
      },
      {
        "title": "English Energy Card Checklist, v2.3 (an Elite Fourum member's spreadsheet, last updated 18 October 2020)",
        "url": "https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1gbLJ3eqF6gyawMy5VJGJxHeBxEGAI-Md/edit"
      }
    ]
  },
  "tell": {
    "text": "No set symbol or number, and a ©2005 line",
    "sources": [
      {
        "title": "Elite Fourum: Where do setless (c) 2006 EX-era Basic Energy come from?",
        "url": "https://www.elitefourum.com/t/where-do-setless-c-2006-ex-era-basic-energy-come-from/31244"
      },
      {
        "title": "Bulbapedia: Basic Fire Energy (TCG) (Wayback Machine copy, 1 September 2026)",
        "url": "https://web.archive.org/web/20260901020457/https://bulbapedia.bulbagarden.net/wiki/Fire_Energy_(TCG)"
      }
    ]
  },
